  <title>4.16.0: Lesson Overview</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01149</md:content-id>
    <md:title>4.16.0: Lesson Overview</md:title>
    <md:uuid>92ffc292-5cdd-49b0-a344-c5726b9024e9</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section id="sect-00001"><para id="para-00001">In this lesson, you will learn how to explain the difference between an arithmetic and a geometric sequence. You will determine arithmetic sequences that will help you solve real-world problems, such as how much fuel is left in your vehicle or how fast the money in your bank account is increasing.</para>
<para id="para-00002">When you finish this lesson, you will be able to:</para>
<list id="list-00001">
  <item>
    Explain what it means for a sequence to be arithmetic or geometric.
 </item>
</list>
<para id="para-00003">Here are the <emphasis>activities</emphasis> that will help you reach those goals:</para>
<list id="list-00002">
  <item>
    4.16.1: Interpreting Function Notation
 </item>
  <item>
    4.16.2: What Is an Arithmetic Sequence? <list id="list-00003">
    <item>
      4.16.2: Self Check
   </item>
    <item>
      4.16.2: Additional Resources
   </item>
  </list>
 </item>
 
  <item>
    4.16.3: A Sequence Is a Type of Function <list id="list-00004">
    <item>
      4.16.3: Self Check
   </item>
    <item>
      4.16.3: Additional Resources
   </item>
  </list>
 </item>
 
  <item>
    4.16.4: Identify and Generate Sequences
 </item>
</list>
<para id="para-00004">After that, you’ll <emphasis>practice and review</emphasis>.</para>
<list id="list-00005">
  <item>
    4.16.5: Practice
 </item>
  <item>
    4.16.6: Lesson Summary
 </item>
</list></section>
</content>
